  "sourceNotes": [
    "An official NWS Frost Advisory remains active for Boyle County, Kentucky, through 9 AM EDT. No official NWS alert is active for the configured Clemson point; mountain frost and freeze headlines remain outside the corridor.",
    "College of DuPage radar at 7:10 AM EDT showed no organized precipitation over either target region; weak circular returns were non-meteorological ground clutter. Early true-color satellite at 7:11 AM showed generally clear conditions across Kentucky and the western Carolinas, with the offshore upper-low cloud shield east of the target areas.",
    "KCEU still had not reported since 4 PM EDT October 16, so current Upstate conditions use KLQK and KAND. KCEU remains a verification station when official reporting resumes.",
    "Official point forecasts, current observations, office discussions and multi-model guidance agree on a dry pattern and steady warming; no unresolved material source conflict remains.",
    "HRRR, RAP, NAM, NAM 3-km Nest, GFS, GEFS and ECMWF availability was verified from official run directories; College of DuPage panels supplied a common visual source.",
    "Tempest data was not used for Upstate observations, verification, calibration or adjustment.",
    "Official NWS alerts are separate from this independent analysis. Independent hazard probabilities do not constitute watches or warnings."
  ],
